# Server Management Rule

Never start, stop, or restart servers/services unless the user explicitly instructs.

## Prohibited Actions
- Do not start new servers (frontend or backend)
- Do not kill existing servers (frontend or backend)
- Do not restart services (frontend or backend)
- Do not manage server processes in any way

## Rationale
- Save files; changes apply automatically via hot-reload.
- No manual server management is required.

## Scope
- Applies to all servers/services: frontend, backend, production, databases, background processes.

## Note
- Dev environment hot-reloads; code changes apply without intervention.